WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.881 --> 00:00:05.891
In this video, you'll see how your schools are using Fixer Nation this school year.

2
00:00:06.392 --> 00:00:17.482
Select Program Use Report in the menu. The tiles at the top show how many teachers are activated, how many students are enrolled, and how many of them have finished a lesson or game.

3
00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:28.900
Month by month shows students active, activities finished, and how many classrooms used Fixer Nation in at least three different weeks. That's what we call regular use.

4
00:00:29.406 --> 00:00:41.626
The school table has one row for each school. A school with very few students is combined with another, and a school with only a few teachers hides its teacher figures, so no one can be picked out.

5
00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:53.689
Further down, standards coverage shows how many students have practiced each New York benchmark and graduate attribute. The social emotional benchmarks sit under the state's three goals.

6
00:00:54.192 --> 00:01:07.132
How we count explains each number in plain words, and what this report can't tell you. It doesn't measure student outcomes, and Fixer Nation has no demographic information, so you'd pair it with your own data.

7
00:01:07.637 --> 00:01:22.457
To share this with your board or attach it to a grant report, download the CSV, or select Print or save as PDF, at the top of the page. Last school year appears here too, once its totals have been saved.
